"DATA","BH100","0.00","0.30","TOPSOIL: Dark brown slightly gravelly fine to coarse sand with occasional rootlets.","101",""
"DATA","BH100","0.30","0.80","Soft brown slightly gravelly sandy CLAY. Sand is fine to coarse. Gravel is angular to subangular fine to medium of sandstone and mudstone.","220",""
"DATA","BH100","0.80","1.50","Soft brown mottled grey slightly sandy slightly gravelly CLAY. Sand is fine to coarse. Gravel is angular to subrounded fine to coarse of sandstone and mudstone.","220",""
"DATA","BH100","1.50","4.65","Firm greyish brown slightly sandy slightly gravelly CLAY. Sand is fine to coarse. Gravel is angular to subrounded fine to coarse of sandstone and mudstone.","220",""
"DATA","BH100","4.65","6.51","Stiff grey slightly sandy slightly gravelly CLAY with low cobble content. Sand is fine to coarse. Gravel is angular to subrounded fine to coarse of sandstone and mudstone. Cobbles are subangular of sandstone.","224",""
"DATA","BH109","0.00","0.30","TOPSOIL: Dark brown slightly gravelly slightly clayey fine to coarse sand.","101",""
"DATA","BH109","0.30","1.00","Soft brown slightly gravelly sandy CLAY. Sand is fine to coarse. Gravel is angular to subrounded fine to coarse of sandstone and mudstone.","220",""
"DATA","BH109","1.00","2.20","Soft brown mottled grey slightly sandy slightly gravelly CLAY with low cobble content. Sand is fine to coarse. Gravel is angular to subrounded fine to coarse of sandstone and mudstone. Cobbles are subangular to subrounded of sandstone.","224",""
"DATA","BH109","10.40","11.70","Reddish brown slightly gravelly slightly silty fine to coarse SAND. Gravel is subangular to subrounded fine to medium of sandstone and mudstone.","412",""
"DATA","BH109","11.70","13.00","Extremely weak brown mottled white medium grained SANDSTONE. Recovered as subangular coarse gravel and cobble sized fragments.","803",""
"DATA","BH109","13.00","13.18","Extremely weak white stained light brown medium grained SANDSTONE. Recovered as non intact core (fine to coarse sand and subangular fine to coarse gravel sized fragments).","803",""
"DATA","BH109","13.18","13.66","Medium strong thinly laminated white stained light brown medium grained micaceous SANDSTONE. Discontinuities: 1) 10-20 degrees extremely closely to closely spaced undulating rough.","803",""
"DATA","BH109","13.66","15.36","Medium strong thinly laminated white and purple stained light brown medium grained micaceous SANDSTONE. Discontinuities: 1) 0-10 degrees very closely to closely spaced planar rough locally with reddish brown clay infill. 2) 80 degrees widely spaced undulating rough stained reddish brown.","803",""
"DATA","BH109","15.36","17.38","Weak thinly bedded yellowish white medium grained SANDSTONE with rare reddish brown inclusions (2mm x 5mm to 10mm x 12mm) of siltstone. Discontinuities: 1) 0-10 degrees very closely to closely spaced undulating rough with localised brown staining.","803",""
"DATA","BH109","17.38","17.72","Assumed zone of core loss. Weak SANDSTONE. (Driller's description)","803","Driller's description"
"DATA","BH109","17.72","17.92","Weak yellowish white medium grained SANDSTONE with abundant reddish brown inclusions (from 1mm x 1mm to 10mm x 10mm). Discontinuities: 1) 0-10 degrees very closely to closely spaced undulating rough with brown staining.","803",""
"DATA","BH109","17.92","18.16","Strong grey medium grained SANDSTONE.","803",""
"DATA","BH109","18.16","20.40","Extremely weak cream stained reddish brown medium grained SANDSTONE. Recovered as non intact core (fine to coarse sand and subangular fine to coarse gravel sized fragments with low cobble content).","803",""
"DATA","BH109","2.20","8.00","Firm grey slightly sandy slightly gravelly CLAY with low cobble content. Sand is fine to coarse. Gravel is angular to subrounded fine to coarse of sandstone and mudstone. Cobbles are subangular to subrounded of sandstone.","224",""
"DATA","BH109","20.40","20.60","Extremely weak reddish brown medium grained SANDSTONE.","803",""
"DATA","BH109","20.60","21.07","Extremely weak grey stained dark reddish brown MUDSTONE.","801",""
"DATA","BH109","21.07","22.40","Extremely weak light grey stained reddish brown MUDSTONE. Recovered as non intact core (gravelly clay).","801",""
"DATA","BH109","22.40","23.31","Weak thinly laminated greenish grey stained dark reddish brown MUDSTONE. Discontinuities: 1) 0-5 degrees very closely to closely spaced planar smooth with reddish brown staining.","801",""
"DATA","BH109","23.31","23.84","Weak thinly laminated greenish grey stained dark reddish brown MUDSTONE. Recovered as non intact core (angular fine to coarse gravel sized fragments).","801",""
"DATA","BH109","23.84","24.75","Medium strong thinly laminated greenish grey stained dark reddish brown MUDSTONE. Discontinuities: 1) 0-5 degrees very closely to closely spaced planar smooth with reddish brown staining.","801",""
"DATA","BH109","24.75","25.28","Medium strong thinly laminated greenish grey stained dark reddish brown MUDSTONE. Recovered as non intact core (clayey angular fine to coarse gravel sized fragments).","801",""
"DATA","BH109","25.28","27.17","Strong thinly laminated grey silty fine grained micaceous SANDSTONE with closely to medium spaced thick laminations to very thin beds of medium strong thinly laminated grey mudstone. Discontinuities: 1) 10 degrees very closely to closely spaced planar rough locally with reddish brown staining.","803",""
"DATA","BH109","27.17","27.64","Weak thinly laminated black bright COAL. Discontinuities: 1) 0-10 degrees very closely spaced planar rough stepped.","806",""
"DATA","BH109","27.64","28.69","Weak to medium strong thinly laminated black dull and bright COAL. Discontinuities: 1) 0-10 degrees very closely to closely spaced planar rough stepped.","806",""
"DATA","BH109","28.69","29.38","Medium strong thinly laminated grey silty micaceous MUDSTONE with extremely closely spaced thin to thick laminations of cream fine grained sandstone. Discontinuities: 1) 5-15 degrees very closely to closely spaced undulating rough.","801",""
"DATA","BH109","29.38","30.20","Weak thinly laminated dark grey MUDSTONE. Discontinuities: 1) 5-15 degrees very closely to closely spaced planar smooth .","801",""
"DATA","BH109","30.20","30.52","Very weak thinly laminated black bright COAL. Recovered as non intact core (angular fine to coarse gravel and cobble sized fragments).","806",""
